// we should do it on the AST instead? Its simpler!
// the ternary is a little... harder. Perhaps we can log the result
// of the tern?
// the problem, is that we don't want to make it like: if test --> if (loggingfunc(test))
// then we lose all the various ASMs generated. JBAN, JBOR, JMPI, JMPF, JMKN, etc
// only one will be generated.
// so we need to put it in the branch itself
// so... thats not so bad for if/while
// but for ternaries... how?
// log the result?

// Soooo...    if ((f)(a,b)) --> if ((f)(a,b)).flowlog
// so a function that returns the input, after logging the result


function Tran_Flow (TranFunc)
	opt norefcounts
	expect (fn) (node, "Only use this on functions")
	|| msg = node[@thg, "off"]
		msg.ExpectLast
		node.SafeRemove
		(fn is FlowDisabled)

	
insertion
	quietly	({FlowLog.DisabledIncr, (_0), FlowLog.DisabledIncr(-1), rejoin 0})


//	if Options.GenFlowLogCode
